# Lab UI (`apps/lab-ui`)

## Scope

- Next.js App Router only under `src/`. Do not edit `.next/`, `node_modules/`, or build output.
- **Dev only:** start with `./run-lab-ui.sh` or `./run-lab.sh` (`next dev`). Do not default to `npm run build` for checks; use the dev server unless the user requests a production build.
- Browser calls the Lab API via `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE` (default `/lab-api`, proxied to FastAPI). Types and fetch helpers live in `src/lib/api.ts`.

## Structure

| Area | Path |
|------|------|
| Pages | `src/app/**/page.tsx` |
| Shared UI | `src/components/ui/*`, `JobMonitor`, `ArtifactGallery`, `Nav` |
| API client | `src/lib/api.ts`, `src/lib/format.ts` |

## Pages

- **Overview** (`/`) — research loop cards, stats, recent runs.
- **Data** (`/data`) — Optional Nobitex export + browse/download CSVs under `data/` (`GET /api/data/csv-files`, `GET /artifact`).
- **Lab** (`/experiments`) — one page for strategy test and compare, saved pipelines, and compare charts. `/actions` redirects here.
- **New** (`/new`) — opportunity discovery (HL universe or catalog), job monitor, past discovery runs; links to Custom for validation.
- **Custom** (`/custom`) — configure a full pipeline: optional export, multi-dataset, strategy compare (subset / max count), multi-model forecasts (`POST /api/jobs/custom-research`).
- **Optimizer** (`/optimizer`) — Optuna/grid sweeps, batch Optuna on catalog CSVs, HL market research pipelines, stored params, sweep history (`POST /api/jobs/strategy-sweep`, `custom-research`, `pipeline-run`).
- **Live** (`/live`) — Hyperliquid-first paper/live (`POST /api/jobs/terminal-once`, `terminal-live`); Nobitex spot optional.
- **Strategies** (`/strategies`) — Ephemeral pair/grid/funding paper backtests (`POST /api/strategies/*`); venue matrix from `GET /api/strategies/exchange-catalog`. Rule strategies use **Custom** (`/custom`).
- **Settings** (`/settings`) — Lab API token, Hyperliquid credentials; optional Nobitex (`/api/auth/*`).
- **Research loop** — nav plus overview cards (`WorkflowCards`, `lib/workflow.ts`): Data → Lab → Runs. Do not add a second bar of the same links.
- **Runs** / **Configurations** — read-only catalog views.

## UI conventions

- **Lab API errors:** `fetchJson` in `api.ts` parses JSON `error` / `detail`. Use `ErrorState` for query failures and `JobErrorAlert` for mutation/job POST errors (both show a Settings link on 401). `LabAuthBanner` in the root layout warns when `LAB_API_TOKEN` is set but `NEXT_PUBLIC_LAB_API_TOKEN` is missing.
- Use existing tokens from `tailwind.config.ts` (`surface`, `panel`, `border`, `accent`, `muted`) and `table.data` / `badge-*` classes in `globals.css`.
- Prefer shared `Card`, `Button`, `Field`, `PageHeader`, `JobMonitor` over one-off styling.
- Charts and downloads use `artifactUrl` / `artifactDownloadUrl`; normalize absolute paths with `normalizeArtifactPath` when reading stored paths.
- Poll job status with React Query (`refetchInterval` while `queued` or `running`); invalidate `runs`, `stats`, `experiments`, `data-csv` on job completion.

## Design system (enforced)

Source of truth: `apps/lab-ui/design-system/traderbot-lab/MASTER.md` — read it before changing layout, colour, or component styling. The `ui-ux-pro-max` skill is installed at `.agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` and `.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/` (`python3 .agents/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py "<query>" --domain ux` for targeted guidance).

- **Tokens only.** Style with `surface` / `panel` / `panel-elevated` / `border` / `border-bright` / `accent` / `on-accent` / `muted` declared in `globals.css`. No raw hex in components.
- **Accent is for interaction only.** Red and green are reserved for PnL and status; never use them as decoration.
- **No AI-slop decoration:** no gradient backgrounds, gradient text, glow shadows, decorative `backdrop-blur`, ambient `blur-3xl` blobs, or hover lift/scale on cards and buttons.
- **Contrast:** normal text ≥ 4.5:1. Primary buttons use `text-on-accent` on `bg-accent` — white on `#5B9AFF` is only 2.8:1.
- **Motion:** 150 ms colour/border transitions, no infinite animations, `prefers-reduced-motion` respected globally.
- **Data:** numeric columns use `tabular-nums`; status must never rely on colour alone.

## Backend pairing

When adding UI features that need new data, extend `lab/` (FastAPI) and document endpoints in `docs/lab.md` — do not call the CLI from the browser.
